From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:21:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 042/131] drm/simpledrm: report the connector as DSI when a
 panel backlight is attached

KWin treats an Unknown connector as an external screen and dims the image
in software instead of using the backlight device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
index 1d40956ce..ec587ec26 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
@@ -834,8 +834,14 @@ static struct simpledrm_device *simpledrm_device_create(struct drm_driver *drv,
 	/* Connector */
 
 	connector = &sdev->connector;
+	/*
+	 * A framebuffer with its own panel backlight is the built-in display;
+	 * report it as such so compositors drive the backlight instead of
+	 * dimming the image. The firmware-set mode is DSI on these phones.
+	 */
 	ret = drm_connector_init(dev, connector, &simpledrm_connector_funcs,
-				 DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_Unknown);
+				 sdev->backlight ? DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DSI :
+						   DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_Unknown);
 	if (ret)
 		return ERR_PTR(ret);
 	drm_connector_helper_add(connector, &simpledrm_connector_helper_funcs);
